\section*{Entropy-rate dimension formula for all real self-similar measures}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
For any finite real self-similar probability measure, its dimension is claimed to equal the smaller of one and map-walk entropy rate divided by Lyapunov exponent, even with exact overlaps and signed unequal contractions. The cited manuscript argues for that result; its relation to this problem is specified below.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Manuscript 1 (family 148, 2026-09-24): Finite-law comparisons expose entropy hidden within grid cells as fair two-point information at finer scales. Blocking and conditioning on symbol counts fixes the composed contractions while preserving map entropy; a hypothetical dimension loss would create too much fair-pair mass in a fine-scale band, contradicting the entropy estimates.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
Manuscript 1 (family 148, 2026-09-24): The problem selects the mathematical statement summarized here, including its stated hypotheses and parameter range. The cited theorem gives a claimed proof of that assertion in full.

\subsection{Formal verification}
For family 148, the scope page documents the following selections. The selected dimension identity permits signed unequal contractions and exact coincidences. Further declarations treat homogeneous measures and overlap-free attractors; density and absolute continuity are not selected. The documented statement covers the main claim of manuscript 1. Comparator files: SelfSimilar.lean, SelfSimilarCorollaries.lean. Declarations: OAI.EntropyRateDimension.entropy\_rate\_dimension, OAI.EntropyRateDimension.Extensions.homogeneous\_dimension\_direct, OAI.CorSetReference.cor\_set.

This site has not executed the Lean files or checked their dependencies. These descriptions report the scope of the linked declarations, rather than a new verification of the proofs.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI attributes these results to an internal model. Its release notice cautions that results lacking full formalization can contain mistakes. This site has not independently assessed the proofs; a solved label records the scope of the reported claim.

